    "question": {
      "source_id": "unreconciled:step-q143278",
      "problem": "Given that ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{72}∼N(11,{12}^{2})$ is a random sample of size $72$ from a normal population, calculate $P(10.75<\\overset{―}{X}<11.3).$\n\n*Hint: Value tables of $Φ(z)$ for different values of $z$ are given below, where $Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n| | $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.2\\,$ | $\\,0.5793\\,$ | $\\,0.5832\\,$ | $\\,0.5871\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.3\\,$ | $\\,0.6179\\,$ | $\\,0.6217\\,$ | $\\,0.6255\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.4\\,$ | $\\,0.6554\\,$ | $\\,0.6591\\,$ | $\\,0.6628\\,$ | |  | | $z$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ | $\\,0.08\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-0.3\\,$ | $\\,0.3594\\,$ | $\\,0.3557\\,$ | $\\,0.3520\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.2\\,$ | $\\,0.3974\\,$ | $\\,0.3936\\,$ | $\\,0.3897\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.1\\,$ | $\\,0.4364\\,$ | $\\,0.4325\\,$ | $\\,0.4286\\,$ | |\n| --- | --- | --- |",
      "worked_solution": "If ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a random sample of size $n$ from a normal population, where \n\n$$\n{X}_{i}∼N(\\mu ,{\\sigma }^{2}),\\,1\\le i\\le n,\n$$\n\nthen the sample mean $\\overset{―}{X}$ has the distribution\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{X}∼N(\\mu ,\\frac{{\\sigma }^{2}}{n}).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the distribution of the sample mean $\\overset{―}{X}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{X} & ∼N\\,(11,\\frac{{12}^{2}}{72}) \\\\  & ∼N(11,2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're required to find $P(10.75<\\overset{―}{X}<11.3).$\n\nFirst, we transform $X$ into a standard normal random variable $Z$ by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(10.75<\\overset{―}{X}<11.3) & =P(\\frac{10.75-11}{\\sqrt{2}}<Z<\\frac{11.3-11}{\\sqrt{2}}) \\\\  & =P(-0.18<Z<0.21) \\\\  & =Φ(0.21)-Φ(-0.18)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the tables, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(0.21)=0.5832, \\\\ Φ(-0.18)=0.4286.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(10.75<\\overset{―}{X}<11.3) & =Φ(0.21)-Φ(-0.18) \\\\  & =0.5832-0.4286 \\\\  & =0.1546.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
